<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">11</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vouille"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-vouille.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Vouillé</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 507</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Vouillé was fought in 507 near Poitiers, in western France.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vezeronce"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-vezeronce.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Vézeronce</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 524</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Vézeronce was fought on 25 June 524 near Vézeronce in the Dauphiné, France, between the Franks and the Burgundians.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ad-decimum"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Ad Decimum</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 533</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Ad Decimum was fought on 13 September 533 at the tenth milestone south of Carthage, where the Byzantine general Belisarius defeated the Vandal army of…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tricamarum"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Tricamarum</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 533</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Tricamarum was fought in December 533 west of Carthage, where the Byzantine army of Belisarius defeated the Vandal king Gelimer and his brother Tzazon…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-shayuan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-shayuan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Shayuan</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 537</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Shayuan was fought in 537 between the Eastern Wei under Gao Huan and the Western Wei under Yuwen Tai, near the Wei River in modern Shaanxi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mons-lactarius"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-mons-lactarius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Mons Lactarius</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 552 or 553</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Mons Lactarius was fought near Mount Vesuvius in Campania in 552 or 553 between the Byzantine army of Narses and the last Ostrogothic king, Teia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-taginae"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-taginae.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Taginae</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 552</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Taginae, also called Busta Gallorum, was fought in the Apennines of central Italy in the summer of 552.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gwansan-fortress"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Gwansan Fortress</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 554</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Gwansan Fortress was fought in 554 near present-day Okcheon in South Korea between Silla and an army of Baekje and its Gaya allies.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gwansanseong"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Gwansanseong</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 554</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Gwansanseong was fought in 554 at the fortress of Gwansanseong, near modern Okcheon in Korea, between Baekje and Silla.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dyrham"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-dyrham.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Dyrham</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 577</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Deorham was fought in 577 at Dyrham, north of Bath in Gloucestershire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dun-bolg"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Dún Bolg</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 598</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Dún Bolg was fought in Leinster in 598, when Brandub mac Echach, king of Leinster and of the Uí Chennselaig, defeated the Uí Néill high king Áed mac…</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Sieges <span class="n">1</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-yubi"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Yubi</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 546</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Yubi was Gao Huan's siege of the Western Wei fortress of Yubi, in modern Jishan county, Shanxi, in 546.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Wars &amp; campaigns <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/vandalic-war"><span class="enc-name">Vandalic War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 533–534</span><span class="enc-snip">The Vandalic War was fought in 533–534 between the Byzantine Empire of Justinian I and the Vandal Kingdom in North Africa.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gothic-war-535-554"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gothic-war-535-554.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gothic War (535–554)</span><span class="enc-type">War · 535–554</span><span class="enc-snip">The Gothic War was fought from 535 to 554 between the Byzantine Empire of Justinian I and the Ostrogothic Kingdom of Italy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/lazic-war"><span class="enc-name">Lazic War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 541–562</span><span class="enc-snip">The Lazic War was fought from 541 to 562 between the Byzantine Empire and the Sasanian Empire for control of Lazica, the kingdom of the Lazi on the eastern Black Sea…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-sasanian-destruction-of-the-hephthalites"><span class="enc-name">Göktürk–Sasanian destruction of the Hephthalites</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · c. 557 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Göktürk–Sasanian destruction of the Hephthalites was a joint campaign around 557 CE that ended the Hephthalite empire in Central Asia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-conquest-of-yemen"><span class="enc-name">Sasanian conquest of Yemen</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · c. 570–578 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sasanian conquest of Yemen was the campaign of c. 570–578 CE in which a Persian expeditionary force expelled the Aksumite-backed regime from South Arabia.</span></a></li></ul></section>
